Final follow-up: the prior recommendation to silently skip required review when Git fails is rejected; the user forbids waived acceptance checks. However, the reported resume dead-end was real. The scheduler now settles no-ready plans as done only if non-empty and all steps done/skipped, otherwise paused. The review gate recognizes skipped steps retaining successful mutation results, so resume cannot bypass review. A real scheduler test proves a failed Git probe, pause, resume, no repeated mutation, and successful review. Unexpected scheduler throws now publish their full current checkpoint before propagating, retaining exports on transition failures. Normal legacy raw event parity remains unchanged. Tests strengthen callback sealing, exact failed and paused cycle-2 wording, recovery warning, actual sequential imported context. A source mutation removes the history reporter guard and is killed. Check concrete remaining defects in these changes. Do not recommend passing a required verification gate when its evidence probe failed.

